Description: Make the extract and analyze doctests self-contained
 The doctests for Binwalk::extract and Binwalk::analyze scan
 /usr/share/man/man2/accept.2.gz, which only exists when manpages-dev happens
 to be installed, so they fail in a clean build chroot. Both also use and
 delete the same /tmp/foobar directory, so they can race with each other when
 doctests run in parallel.
 .
 Generate a small gzip file with flate2 (already a dependency) in a temporary
 directory unique to each doctest, and point the examples at it. The examples
 still exercise scanning and extraction as before.
 .
 Upstream reworked these doctests after 3.1.0 (commit ec3a7b76196ab9a1bc93260160eab6721801e7ed),
 but that version reads tests/inputs/gzip.bin, which is not shipped in the
 crate, so it cannot be used here.
Author: Fukui Daichi <a.dog.will.talk@akane.waseda.jp>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
